      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Objective",
          "content": "To elicit patient stakeholders' experience and perspectives about patient-centred care."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Design",
          "content": "Qualitative."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Setting",
          "content": "A large urban healthcare system."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Participants",
          "content": "Four patient stakeholders who are prostate cancer survivors."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Main outcome measures",
          "content": "Experience and perspectives of patient stakeholders regarding patient-centred care and treatment decisions."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Results",
          "content": "Our patient stakeholders represented a diverse socio-demographic group. The patient stakeholders identified engagement and dialogue with physicians as crucial elements of patient-centred care model. The degree of patient-centred care was observed to be dependent on the situations. High severity conditions warranted a higher level of patient involvement, compared to mild conditions. They agreed that patient-centred care should not mean that patients can demand inappropriate treatments."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "Conclusions",
          "content": "An important attribute of patient-centred outcomes research model is the involvement of stakeholders. However, we have limited knowledge about the experience of patient stakeholders in patient-centred outcomes research. Our study indicates that patient stakeholders offer a unique perspective as researchers and policy-makers aim to precisely define patient-centred research and care."
        }
      ]},
